message: "If you use this search engine, its results or its methods, please cite it as below."
title: "Numbers palindromic in bases 2, 10 and 16: exhaustive search below 2^472"
authors:
  - family-names: Atrey
    given-names: Mudit
date-released: 2026-11-22
version: "1.0"
url: "https://github.com/MuditAtrey/palindromes-2-10-16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MuditAtrey/palindromes-2-10-16"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - palindromes
  - number theory
  - multi-base palindromes
  - exhaustive search
  - OEIS A007632
  - OEIS A029731
  - OEIS A340559
abstract: >-
  An exhaustive, integer-only search showing that no integer N with 9 < N < 2^472 is a palindrome in bases 2, 10 and 16
  at the same time, with the search engine (tripal), its 47-test suite, planted-solution controls, a timestamped
  commitment, and research notes on why no known proof method covers every length.
